1. Introduction and Motivation}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\cf1\insrsid16668280 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa120\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\cf1\insrsid16668280 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
Postpartum Depression (PPD) is a common but under-diagnosed mental health condition affecting mothers after childbirth. In Bangladesh, screening relies primarily on clinical instruments such as\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
 the Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale (EPDS) and the Patient Health Questionnaire-9 (PHQ-9), both of which require a trained interviewer and are not applied universally. A machine learning model that can flag high-risk mothers using only routinely-col
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 l\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 ectable demographic, economic, family, and pregnancy-history information -- without requiring the EPDS/PHQ-9 interview itself -- could support earlier, more scalable screening.
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 An existing external study on a similar Bangladesh dataset reports near-perfect\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
 discrimination (AUROC), which is a strong indicator of data leakage: the model was very likely trained using answers to the EPDS/PHQ-9 items themselves (or scores derived from them) as predictors of a label that is directly computed from those same items
.\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37  Such a model cannot be deployed in practice, because at prediction time a mother who has not yet completed an EPDS/PHQ-9 interview has none of those answers available.
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 This project builds a machine learning framework that is explicitly designed to avoid t\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
his failure mode, while introducing a genuine methodological contribution -- four engineered Composite Risk Indices -- and a thorough, multi-angle explainability analysis so that the model's predictions can be trusted and clinically interpreted rather tha
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 n\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37  treated as a black box.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\cf1\insrsid16668280 \page }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43\afs30 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\fs30\cf19\insrsid16668280 \hich\af43\dbch\af31505\loch\f43 
2. Dataset Description}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\cf1\insrsid16668280 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa120\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\cf1\insrsid16668280 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
The dataset is the Mendeley "Data for Postpartum Depression Prediction in Bangladesh" dataset: 800 postpartum mothers, 70 raw columns (69 after removing a redundant index column). It contains demographic, ec\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
onomic, family/social, pregnancy, delivery, neonatal, and prior mental-health-history questions, plus the 10 EPDS items and 9 PHQ-9 items used to compute two clinical scores and their corresponding severity categories.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa60\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\cf1\insrsid16668280 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Column roles}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\cf1\insrsid16668280 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa120\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\cf1\insrsid16668280 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 - Target candidates: EPD\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
S Score, EPDS Result (Low/Medium/High), PHQ9 Score, PHQ9 Result (Minimal/Mild/Moderate/Moderately Severe/Severe), and an engineered binary target PPD_binary (EPDS Score >= 13 -> 1, following the convention used in the reference literature).
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 - Leakage colum\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 ns (23 total, never used as model input): the 10 EPDS items, the 9 PHQ-9 items, and the 4 score/category columns they produce.
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 - Safe input features (46 raw columns): demographic, family, economic, pregnancy, delivery, neonatal, and prior (pre-postpartum) \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
mental-health-history questions -- none of which are derived from the EPDS/PHQ-9 interview itself.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa60\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\cf1\insrsid16668280 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 Target class distributions (n = 800)}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 
