\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa120\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \f37\cf1\insrsid16668280 \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
- The "Abuse" survey question's real-world meaning needs verification against the original Bangla questionnaire wording, since its empirical direction (No answers associating with higher PPD) is counter-intuitive and consistent
\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 ly reproduced across three independent methods, suggesting either a genuine but unusual finding or a translation/coding nuance rather than a modeling artifact.
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 - With n = 800 and, for PHQ9 Result, 5 imbalanced classes, statistical power for some comparison\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
s (e.g. the original 5-fold ablation significance test) is limited; this was mitigated but not eliminated by the repeated-CV re-test.
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 - The error analysis identified a specific, characterized blind spot: mothers whose survey answers do not outwardly match \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
the "typical" risk profile (low apparent mental-health risk, decent apparent support) despite genuinely meeting clinical PPD criteria are the mothers the model is most likely to miss.
\par \hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 - All results are internal, cross-validated estimates on a single-countr\hich\af37\dbch\af31505\loch\f37 
y, single-dataset sample; external validation on an independent Bangladeshi (or other South Asian) cohort would be needed before any clinical deployment claim.
